Enable Acima Digital's lease-to-own payment option for your WooCommerce store.

== Description ==

The Acima Digital Payment Gateway integrates seamlessly with WooCommerce to offer your customers a flexible and secure
alternative payment solution. This plugin provides our merchant partners everything needed to start accepting Acima
Digital payments on their website.

Acima's eCommerce lease-to-own solution empowers customers to shop for the items they want, all without credit.

On average, retailers that use Acima experience:

* Less cart abandonment
* Up to 30% more sales
* Up to 2x ticket size
* Higher approval rates

Not an Acima partner? [Apply here](https://acimacredit.my.site.com/retailerapplication/?utm_medium=web-b&utm_source=partner-page&utm_content=become-partner-button&dasrc=web&davuid=5751731434172716)
Need more information? Visit [www.acima.com](https://www.acima.com)

= Key Features =
* Seamless WooCommerce integration
* Support for block-based checkout
* Comprehensive order management
* Secure payment processing
* Full refund support

== Installation ==

1. Download the zipped file by clicking the download button.
2. Go to your WordPress Admin Dashboard.
3. Navigate to the Plugins page.
4. Click on "Upload Plugin" and select the file you downloaded in step 1 (acima-leasing-payment-gateway.zip). (Note: do not unzip or extract the file before you upload it).
5. Click on "Activate".

= Configure the Plugin =
1. Go to the WooCommerce Settings page and navigate to the "Payments" tab.
2. Select "Acima Leasing" in the payment method options.
3. Click on "Enable Acima Leasing".
4. Fill out the API URL, Merchant ID, Acima API URL, Acima Client ID, and Acima Client Secret fields (Note: Please send an email to integration.support@acima.com to request information for these fields).
5. Click "Save changes" to activate the plugin.

== Frequently Asked Questions ==

= Is this compatible with WooCommerce Blocks? =
Yes, the plugin fully supports both traditional and block-based checkout experiences.

= How do I test the integration? =
Acima provides a sandbox environment for testing. Configure the plugin with your test credentials and use test customer data provided by Acima.

= What happens if an order is refunded? =
The plugin handles full and partial refunds through WooCommerce's standard refund interface, automatically notifying Acima's system.

= How secure is the payment process? =
All sensitive data is handled directly by Acima's secure systems. The plugin uses OAuth 2.0 for API authentication and follows WordPress security best practices.

